<title>UK: Bass falls after negative press report.</title>
<headline>Bass falls after negative press report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Bass Plc fell on Friday after an article in the Evening Standard newspaper said the company could abandon its planned takeover of Carlsberg-Tetley because of conditions imposed by the Office of Fair Trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>Bass shares fell 11p to 783-1/2p by 1625 GMT.  </p>
<p>The report said that some industry observers suggested the conditions laid down by the Office of Fair Trading (OFT) were &quot;so draconian&quot; that the takeover may be aborted.</p>
<p>Dealers said negative comment from brokerage Kleinwort Benson, which yesterday repeated a &quot;sell&quot; recommendation ahead of the company's results next week, added to the weakness in the share price.  </p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Bass said the company had no comment on the report and said the takeover process was confidential.</p>
<p>--Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
